    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31861" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obsĭdĭōnālis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		obsidio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a
			siege</i>: corona, <i>a crown of grass, granted as a
				reward to a general who rescued others from siege</i>, Paul. ex
				<i><span class="en">Fest. p. 190</span></i> Müll.; so <i><span class="en">Liv. 7, 37,
				2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 22, 4, 4, § 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 5, 6,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aur. Vict. Vir. Ill. 59</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">machinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 24, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">morae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Strat. 1, 3, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mala,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
